# Unisoc (SPRD) dma-buf / ION pieces.

config SPRD_ION
	tristate "Unisoc ION allocator"
	help
	  Vendor ION allocator for Unisoc UMS512/T618 (sprd_ion.c). Provides
	  sprd_ion_get_buffer() / sprd_ion_get_phys_addr() / sprd_ion_free_buffer()
	  used by the VSP (vsp_common.c), CPP (cpp_core.c) and JPG (sprd_jpg)
	  drivers -- all three `select SPRD_ION`.

	  DECLARED 2026-10-09: before this the symbol had NO definition in any
	  Kconfig, so `select SPRD_ION` from the consumers selected an implicit
	  symbol that olddefconfig/syncconfig silently DROPS from .config
	  (undeclared symbols are not written to auto.conf), and the Makefile's
	  obj-$(CONFIG_SPRD_ION) then built nothing. Symptom on the device
	  build: ion built only while a hand-appended CONFIG_SPRD_ION=y survived
	  in .config; every kconfig pass removed it and sprd_ion.o stopped
	  building, leaving the consumers with unresolved symbols.

	  Say M to build the module, or Y to link it into the kernel.

config ION_IPC_TRUSTY
	tristate "Unisoc ION <-> Trusty IPC client"
	depends on TRUSTY_VIRTIO_IPC
	help
	  Transport adapter between the Unisoc ION allocator and the Trusty TEE.
	  Ports the vendor blob ion_ipc_trusty.ko: it opens the TIPC channel
	  "com.android.trusty.ion" and forwards ION messages to the secure world.

	  This module is a pure CLIENT of the tipc_chan_* API. It provides no
	  ION allocation itself and needs no ION core, so it is independent of
	  CONFIG_SPRD_ION (declared in this file since 2026-10-09; before that
	  it had no definition, and ION itself was removed from mainline).

	  The protocol was recovered from the vendor blob with radare2 and
	  Ghidra; see drivers/dma-buf/sprd/ion_ipc_trusty.c for the provenance
	  and for the three deliberate deviations from the blob.

	  Say M to build the module (recommended while it is unproven at
	  runtime), or Y to link it into the kernel. Say N if unsure.
